[38;5;231m⏺[39m I renamed the field, but there's a conflict you should know about before this goes anywhere.

  The change is one line in [38;5;153mroutes/users.js:6[39m, from [38;5;153muserId: u.id[39m to [38;5;153muser_id: u.id[39m. Nothing else in the repo uses [38;5;153muserId[39m.
  It isn't committed.

  [1mThe conflict:[0m the README says the web app, the iOS app (3.2 and later) and the nightly partner export all consume [38;5;153mGET
[39m  [38;5;153m/users[39m. It also says field names in the response are part of the contract and that changes go through a versioned
  endpoint. Renaming the field in place would break all three as soon as it ships, because they'd look for [38;5;153muserId[39m and
  not find it.

  Some ways forward:
  1. [1mVersioned endpoint:[0m add something like [38;5;153mGET /v2/users[39m that returns [38;5;153muser_id[39m, and leave [38;5;153m/users[39m unchanged. This is the
